          "kind": "informational",
          "level": "none",
          "guid": "ms5tdp1t5dl52zbw",
          "message": {
            "text": "These assert the computed border-left-color, not the class name, because the class landing without a matching CSS rule is the exact half-fix that still leaves the user with nothing to see.\n\n.ticket-row had &.blocked in SCSS; .column-card did not. A class-presence assertion would have passed on a card that renders identically to an unblocked one.\n\nVerified the spec catches the real bug: with the blocked / feedback-needed classes removed from createColumnCard and the client rebuilt, exactly one test fails —\n\n1 failed\n  [chromium] › e2e/blocked-indicator.spec.ts:75:3 › column-view card shows the blocked border too\n2 passed (22.5s)\n\nThe list-view and precedence tests still pass there, which is the right discrimination: they cover a surface that was already correct, and only the column-view assertion is load-bearing for this fix.\n",
            "markdown": "These assert the computed `border-left-color`, not the class name, because the class landing without a matching CSS rule is the exact half-fix that still leaves the user with nothing to see.\n\n`.ticket-row` had `&.blocked` in SCSS; `.column-card` did not. A class-presence assertion would have passed on a card that renders identically to an unblocked one.\n\nVerified the spec catches the real bug: with the `blocked` / `feedback-needed` classes removed from `createColumnCard` and the client rebuilt, exactly one test fails —\n\n```\n1 failed\n  [chromium] › e2e/blocked-indicator.spec.ts:75:3 › column-view card shows the blocked border too\n2 passed (22.5s)\n```\n\nThe list-view and precedence tests still pass there, which is the right discrimination: they cover a surface that was already correct, and only the column-view assertion is load-bearing for this fix.\n"
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "e2e/blocked-indicator.spec.ts"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 13,
                  "endLine": 17,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "\n/** `--blocked: #4b5563` (styles.scss) — the dark-gray blocked accent. */\nconst BLOCKED_RGB = 'rgb(75, 85, 99)';\n/** `--star: #eab308` — the gold up-next accent, for the precedence check. */\nconst STAR_RGB = 'rgb(234, 179, 8)';"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          ],
